From: Runeon Contributors <dev@runeon.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mmdevapi: Log the code and status of a failed driver Unix call.

wine_unix_call() asserts that the driver Unix call returned
STATUS_SUCCESS. The audio drivers report device errors through the
result field of their parameters and return STATUS_SUCCESS themselves,
so a non-zero status normally means the call did not complete: a fault
in the Unix library during the call comes back from the syscall
dispatcher as the exception code. The assertion message only names
mmdevapi_private.h, which tells neither which call failed nor how.

Before the assertion, log the driver name, the call code and the
status on the default err channel. The assertion and everything else
are unchanged, so behaviour is identical; the only difference is one
log line on a path that aborts the process anyway.

diff --git a/dlls/mmdevapi/main.c b/dlls/mmdevapi/main.c
index 66a6327..ffcdb13 100644
--- a/dlls/mmdevapi/main.c
+++ b/dlls/mmdevapi/main.c
@@ -51,6 +51,13 @@ WINE_DEFAULT_DEBUG_CHANNEL(mmdevapi);
 DriverFuncs drvs;
 static DriverFuncs midi_driver;
 
+/* The assertion that follows only names the header; log which call failed
+ * and how, since a fault in the Unix library comes back as its status. */
+void unix_call_failed(unsigned int code, NTSTATUS status)
+{
+    ERR("%s unix call %u failed, status %#lx\n", wine_dbgstr_w(drvs.module_name), code, status);
+}
+
 #define MIDI_CALL(code,args)  __wine_unix_call( midi_driver.module_unixlib, code, args )
 
 const WCHAR drv_keyW[] = L"Software\\Wine\\Drivers";
diff --git a/dlls/mmdevapi/mmdevapi_private.h b/dlls/mmdevapi/mmdevapi_private.h
index 672d901..4dbb7d0 100644
--- a/dlls/mmdevapi/mmdevapi_private.h
+++ b/dlls/mmdevapi/mmdevapi_private.h
@@ -114,9 +114,12 @@ typedef struct MMDevice {
     struct list entry;
 } MMDevice;
 
+extern void unix_call_failed(unsigned int code, NTSTATUS status);
+
 static inline void wine_unix_call(const unsigned int code, void *args)
 {
     const NTSTATUS status = __wine_unix_call(drvs.module_unixlib, code, args);
+    if (status) unix_call_failed(code, status);
     assert(!status);
 }
 
